; The C flags of every library, test and bench under dev/device. A stanza
; names no C flag of its own.
;
; A C warning is an error in every profile but release, as in nx: a release
; build must not break on a warning a future compiler adds.
;
; The sanitize profile compiles the C with AddressSanitizer and
; UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer and links the sanitizer runtimes into every
; executable, whose link_flags keep :standard to carry them. Its options are
; CI's, so a local run fails where CI does: a report ends the process, leaks
; are not errors, and a domain's thread exits on the signal stack the OCaml
; runtime allocated, which AddressSanitizer would unmap as its own.
;
; Benches are not attached to runtest: run them with `dune build @bench`, or
; run a built exe from its directory under _build/default. Every bench rule
; takes the workspace lock %{workspace_root}/bench, because suites running at
; once contend for cores and distort each other's numbers.
;
; A bench's C that calls a library's C sits in a library of its own: a static
; link lists a library's archives after the executable's objects, dependents
; before dependencies, so GNU ld finds the symbols in the library's archive;
; stubs of the executable itself would come after it, too late for GNU ld.
;
; WINDTRAP_TIMEOUT bounds each test that sets no ~timeout of its own: the
; watch server is shared, and a test that never ends blocks every build.

(env
 (release
  (c_flags
   (:standard -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra))
  (env-vars
   (WINDTRAP_TIMEOUT 60)))
 (sanitize
  (c_flags
   (:standard
    -std=c11
    -Wall
    -Wextra
    -Werror
    -g
    -fno-omit-frame-pointer
    -fsanitize=address,undefined))
  (link_flags
   (:standard -cclib -fsanitize=address,undefined))
  (env-vars
   (ASAN_OPTIONS halt_on_error=1:detect_leaks=0:use_sigaltstack=0)
   (UBSAN_OPTIONS halt_on_error=1:print_stacktrace=1)
   (WINDTRAP_TIMEOUT 60)))
 (_
  (c_flags
   (:standard -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror))
  (env-vars
   (WINDTRAP_TIMEOUT 60))))
